     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">\r\n<div>Hi All</div>\r\n<div>Following Perry&#39;s note about the Nimble article I thought I should also mention </div>\r\n<div>the tutorial article published by Spatial and Spatio Temporal Epidemiology (Elsevier)</div>\r\n<div><i>Lawson A. B. (2020)</i><i> </i><i>Nimble for Bayesian Disease Mapping </i></div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>Available from </div>\r\n<div><a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1877584520300010\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1877584520300010&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187518000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3XiSdrew7_aapklq2SMREq\"><font color=\"#0563C1\"><u>https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1877584520300010</u></font></a></div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>For anyone interested in Nimble applications in disease mapping.</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>best</div>\r\n<div>Andrew</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>Division of Biostatistics and Bioinformatics</div>\r\n<div>Department of Public Health Sciences</div>\r\n<div>Medical University of South Carolina</div>\r\n<div>Charleston</div>\r\n<div>29425</div>\r\n<div>South Carolina</div>\r\n<div>USA</div>\r\n<div>ph: <a href=\"tel:(843)%20876-1865\" value=\"+18438761865\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">843-876-1865</a></div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>new 3rd edition of BDM book:</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div><a href=\"http://www.crcpress.com/9781138575424\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.crcpress.com/9781138575424&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187518000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20q5EaKAvgdYjZBSYEjPx8\"><font color=\"#0563C1\"><u>www.crcpress.com/9781138575424</u></font></a> </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>Handbook of Spatial Epidemiology:</div>\r\n<div> <