     "<div><div>\r\n            <div style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#26282a\">\r\n                \r\n                <div>\r\n                    On Thursday, 20 February 2020, 15:20:44 WET, Perry de Valpine &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pdeva...@berkeley.edu</a>&gt; wrote:\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div><br></div>\r\n                <div><br></div>\r\n                <div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Rui!<div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div>We occasionally (every week or two) tweet (none of us are major twitter people!) about a nimble use case.</div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div>Our two most recent were your paper (<a shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1225830992935448576\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1225830992935448576&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YUWBjTWHdz9bvXREVNf0C\">https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1225830992935448576</a>) and Andrew&#39;s paper (<a shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1229464520529080320\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1229464520529080320&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XRb7qcETkg4_JDOQDusgG\">https://twitter.com/R_nimble/status/1229464520529080320</a>).</div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div></div><br clear=\"none\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wed, Feb 19, 2020 at 11:54 PM Rui Martins &lt;<a shape=\"rect\" href rel=\"nofollow\" data-email-masked>ruicost...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br clear=\"none\"></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi nimble community,</div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div>thanks for the information about new examples using nimble.<br clear=\"none\"></div><div>If you allow me, I will add another one:<br clear=\"none\"></div><div>A paper considering joint models with spatial random-effects is available from here:</div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div><h1><span>Improving teeth aesthetics using a spatially shared-parameters model for independent regular lattices</span></h1><span></span><ul><li>\r\n<a shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/02664763.2020.1724273\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1080/02664763.2020.1724273&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DLEM1DU9ff0Ch1QuXGhvH\">https://doi.org/10.1080/02664763.2020.1724273</a></li></ul><div>Thanks</div><div>Rui<br clear=\"none\"></div></div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><br clear=\"none\">segunda-feira, 17 de Fevereiro de 2020 às 17:51:57 UTC, pdevalpine escreveu:<blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Andrew.  That&#39;s great to see.<div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div>(Unfortunately the University of California is in a massive conflict with Elsevier; <a shape=\"rect\" href=\"https://osc.universityofcalifornia.edu/uc-publisher-relationships/uc-and-elsevier/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://osc.universityofcalifornia.edu/uc-publisher-relationships/uc-and-elsevier/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478187526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0cNStZOElh5pVdG403qhuJ\">https://osc.universityofcalifornia.edu/uc-publisher-relationships/uc-and-elsevier/</a>).</div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div><div>-Perry</div></div><br clear=\"none\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sat, Feb 15, 2020 at 8:01 AM Lawson, Andrew B. &lt;<a shape=\"rect\" rel=\"nofollow\">laws...@musc.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br clear=\"none\"></div><blockquote style=\"marg